# Node compile-cache directory that a Windows checkout committed by accident:
# 597 files, 2.8 MB. The real directory name is NOT "C:\Users\..." — the drive
# colon and backslashes were committed as private-use Unicode look-alikes
# (U+F03A, U+F05C), which is why a plain "CUsersKLINTK*" glob does not match it
# (the stale .dockerignore rule had exactly that bug). Match on the segment that
# is real ASCII instead.
**/node-compile-cache/
prototype/C*Users*KLINTK*
